+    <h2>Reading without an account</h2>
+    <p>The DevTools Times is a demonstration news application. You can read articles without signing up or signing in. Visiting a page does not initialize a reading-list session; saving an article uses session state to remember your reading list.</p>
+
+    <h2 id="accounts">Account forms</h2>
+    <p>Signing up sends only the username and password you enter to create a demo account. Signing in sends the same two fields to check your credentials. Both requests go directly over HTTPS to an external authentication service hosted on Google Cloud Functions at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net/times_cdn/api</code>, using the <code>/register</code> or <code>/login</code> endpoint. This happens only when you submit the form.</p>
+    <p>The service receives your credentials and network information such as your IP address. Requests omit cookies and referrer information and are not cached by this frontend. The forms do not log credentials or save credentials or returned tokens in browser storage. Password fields are cleared after every submission attempt. Your browser or password manager may offer to save credentials under your own settings.</p>
+    <p>The demo checks the service response but does not establish a signed-in session. The external service's storage practices, retention periods, and account access, correction, and deletion procedures have not been verified in this application. Use a non-identifying username and a unique demo password; do not submit personal information or credentials used elsewhere. These service practices need to be verified before real accounts are offered.</p>
+
+    <h2 id="third-parties">Third-party resources</h2>
+    <p>The shared page layout does not load third-party analytics, advertising scripts, or remote fonts. There is no optional tracking to enable in this layout. Some articles contain externally hosted images; loading those resources exposes network information to their hosts. The site suppresses referrer information, but this does not hide your IP address from services you contact.</p>
+
+    <h2>Browser privacy controls</h2>
+    <p>Document responses disable unused camera, microphone, location, motion sensor, payment, and USB permissions. Account pages are marked no-store. These controls reduce unnecessary exposure; they do not determine how the hosting infrastructure or external authentication service retains server logs.</p>
